{"contract":"bw-jmdict-shard/3","entries":[{"accent":1,"common":true,"examples":[{"en":"When I visited my friend in Nagano, I was treated to delicious soba.","ja":"長野にいる友人を訪問した際、おいしいそばをごちそうになった。","ref":"278139_125853","source":"tanaka"},{"en":"When I visited my friend in Nagoya, I was treated to delicious soba.","ja":"名古屋に住む友人を訪ねた時、おいしいそばをおごってもらった。","ref":"261901_152648","source":"tanaka"},{"en":"I had a bowl of noodles at a street nearby.","ja":"すぐそこでそばを立ち食いしてきた。","ref":"52277_214981","source":"tanaka"},{"en":"Soba is made of buckwheat flour, and udon and kishimen are made of plain wheat flour.","ja":"そばはそば粉から、うどんやきしめんは普通の小麦粉からできてるの。","ref":"327107_76613","source":"tanaka"}],"forms":["蕎麦"],"glosses":["buckwheat (Fagopyrum esculentum)","soba","Japanese buckwheat noodles","Chinese-style wheat noodles"],"id":"1238460","lemma":"蕎麦","pos":["n"],"readingKata":"ソバ","readings":["そば","そばむぎ","そまむぎ","ソバ"]},{"accent":0,"common":false,"forms":["蕎麦殻","そば殻"],"glosses":["buckwheat chaff"],"id":"1238470","lemma":"蕎麦殻","pos":["n"],"readingKata":"ソバガラ","readings":["そばがら"]},{"accent":0,"common":false,"etymology":[],"examples":[{"en":"It is better to be stung by a nettle than pricked by a rose.","ja":"バラのとげで刺されるよりは、いらくさのとげで刺された方がましだ。","ref":"35086_197897","source":"tanaka"}],"forms":["刺草","蕁麻"],"glosses":["Urtica thunbergiana (species of stinging nettle)"],"id":"1306600","lemma":"刺草","pos":["n"],"readingKata":"イラクサ","readings":["いらくさ","イラクサ","じんま","おいら"],"sourceUrls":["https://zh.wiktionary.org/wiki/いらくさ#Japanese","https://kaikki.org/zhwiktionary/All%20languages%20combined/meaning/い/いら/いらくさ.html"],"synonyms":[],"zhGlosses":["〈植〉荨麻。","刺草redirected from 蕁麻","蕁麻alt-of蕁麻alternative kanji"],"zhSenses":[{"examples":[],"glosses":["〈植〉荨麻。"],"pos":""},{"examples":[],"glosses":["刺草redirected from 蕁麻"],"pos":"non-lemma"},{"examples":[],"glosses":["蕁麻alt-of蕁麻alternative kanji"],"pos":"non-lemma"}]},{"accent":0,"common":false,"forms":["蕉風"],"glosses":["correct style in a haiku (like Basho's)"],"id"